**Theorem 7.2 (complete current continuation, exact in A and set-valued
in C).** Suppose a settled current state has any $t\in\mathcal D$ and
any $x\in\mathbb Q^{V_t}$, with its earned current correspondence and
the actual backed context of Assumption 2.3. Retain a predicted pair
$(\widehat t,\widehat x)=(t,x)$, and in C the digital contract of §8.
For every finite sufficiently backed adaptive continuation, an installed
finite controller maintains this equality at each completed settled cut.
It predicts each full deterministic response in A and each full set of
allowed digital responses in C, consumes the actual response, and
maintains the following actual successors:

| Complete semantic case | Actual successor and reply |
| --- | --- |
| Reset | $(t,0)$; fixed acknowledgement |
| valid Add$(j,q)$ | $(t,x+qe_{\ell_j})$; fixed acknowledgement |
| Tick | $(t,T_tx)$; fixed acknowledgement |
| Hold | $(t,x)$; fixed acknowledgement |
| valid A Read$(j)$ | $(t,x)$; literal rational $x_{\ell_j}$ |
| valid C Read$(j,p)$ | $(t,x)$; an actual integer in the two-element set (8.1) |
| enabled A growth $g:t\to t'$ | $(t',\iota_gx)$; complete raw Growth |
| enabled C growth $g:t\to t'$ | $(t',T_{t'}\iota_gx)$; consumed inner Growth/Tick acknowledgement and complete outward Growth |
| absent, branch or wrong-type growth | unchanged; its distinct refusal, with no Tick |
| otherwise valid out-of-roster integer Add/Read | unchanged; RangeRefusal |
| malformed or noncanonical complete frame | unchanged; BadFrame |

Proper prefixes and disabled calls have exactly Definition 7.1's
pending/enabledness behavior, not an invented completed table row.

**Proof.** AAII Theorem 89.2 already proves this invariant and its
acquired-frame implementation for the exact field menu and the raw or
post-clock material edits. Here A uses its raw zero-extension row with
law (2.2), and C uses its actual $+$ row with that same law. Geometry,
roster updates, finite navigation, finite rational arithmetic and actual
Return correspond exactly to that supplier. The only changed semantic
row is C Read: its law in §8 leaves the field fixed, predicts its full
two-element set, and consumes the integer actually returned. It therefore
preserves the same equality invariant without predicting a hidden bit.

Every other row follows directly from the actual primitive specified in
the table. The deterministic parser and control fields are updated from
the same acquired input and reply bits; a proper prefix remains pending
and a completed call commits at its actual lifecycle completion before
the next Ready. For C growth, the inner new-tree Tick is actually consumed
before committing the outward settled pair. Induction on completed calls, with the pending
prefix behavior between them, covers every finite adaptive continuation.
If a memory block is desired after an update, construct
$O_{I(t')}\widehat x'$ on the earned new tree; its entries are local predictions and its
left inverse still recovers the current field. Their construction and
coexisting old/new stores are paid. $\square$

This theorem permits later Reset, arbitrary rational Add, extra Ticks,
refused probes and arbitrary legal further growth. These continuations
need not remain in either historical image. It is a current-service
theorem, not an inverse for arbitrary old journals, intermediate busy
cuts, interrupted transactions or revoked authority.
Common adaptive continuations use the same accessible side data and, if
used, the same random tape, together with the responses from the current
cut onward. A policy consulting unequal old archives or authority/resource
stores enlarges that task and is not covered by a content-only kernel.

